{
  "id": "wundt-curve",
  "term": "Wundt curve",
  "definition": "The Wundt curve is an inverted U-shaped relation in which moderate arousal potential is linked to the most positive hedonic response, while very low or very high arousal is less pleasant. In this context, arousal potential can come from factors such as novelty, complexity, and uncertainty.",
